Package: GDSAnnotator
Type: Package
Title: Whole-genome variant annotation data manipulation using GDS files
Version: 0.99.1
Date: 2026-09-25
Depends: R (>= 4.6.0), gdsfmt (>= 1.32.0), SeqArray (>= 1.53.2)
Imports: methods, utils, IRanges, GenomicRanges, S4Vectors
Suggests: VariantAnnotation, BiocStyle, knitr, rmarkdown, testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Authors@R: c(person("Xiuwen", "Zheng", role=c("aut", "cre"),
        email="xiuwen.zheng@abbvie.com",
        comment=c(ORCID="0000-0002-1390-0708")),
        person("Yuantao (Raven)", "Chen", role="ctb"),
        person("Hufeng", "Zhou", role="ctb", email="hufengzhou@g.harvard.edu"))
Description: Fast and memory-efficient manipulation of whole-genome variant
        annotation data stored in Genomic Data Structure (GDS) files. Variant
        annotation resources and annotator outputs, including FAVOR, gnomAD,
        Ensembl VEP, SnpEff and ANNOVAR, can be converted into compact
        SeqArray-compatible GDS files that support random access. Variants
        given as chr-pos-ref-alt strings, data frames, GRanges objects, VCF
        files or VCF objects, or SeqArray GDS files can then be annotated by
        querying these files, and the annotations can be written back into a
        GDS file. The
        package also computes summary statistics of the variants and their
        annotations in a single pass over a file, and renders them as a
        VEP/SnpEff-like report, making it a valuable resource for large-scale
        genomic analyses.
